WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.134 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Our next guest is

00:00:01.134 --> 00:00:02.168 line:92%
a voting rights organizer,

00:00:02.168 --> 00:00:04.437 align:start size:94% position:6%
former Georgia
state representative,

00:00:04.437 --> 00:00:05.372 size:88% position:44% line:92%
and best-selling author.

00:00:05.372 --> 00:00:08.608 align:start size:94% position:6%
Her new book,
"While Justice Sleeps,"

00:00:08.608 --> 00:00:09.376 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
is available now.

00:00:09.376 --> 00:00:12.212 align:start size:94% position:6%
Please welcome back
to the show Stacey Abrams.

00:00:12.212 --> 00:00:13.847 align:start size:94% position:6%
Hello, Stacey.
How are you?

00:00:13.847 --> 00:00:15.749 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I am well.
Thank you. How are you?

00:00:15.749 --> 00:00:17.384 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I'm very well.
Your book is called

00:00:17.384 --> 00:00:19.953 size:88% position:44%
"While Justice Sleeps."
Last time you were here,

00:00:19.953 --> 00:00:22.789 align:start size:94% position:6%
it was right before the
runoffs in Georgia.

00:00:22.789 --> 00:00:24.791 size:84% position:42%
Both the candidates,
you were supporting won

00:00:24.791 --> 00:00:26.359 align:start size:94% position:6%
and we talked
about you sleeping

00:00:26.359 --> 00:00:28.695 size:81% position:41%
and I'm just wondering
if you managed to take

00:00:28.695 --> 00:00:33.166
a celebratory nap at the end
of those runoff elections.

00:00:33.166 --> 00:00:34.200 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-I did, indeed.

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:36.736 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I woke up
to voter suppression

00:00:36.736 --> 00:00:38.605 line:92%
coming back in force, so,

00:00:38.605 --> 00:00:41.107 align:start size:94% position:6%
I may not do another nap
for a while.

00:00:41.107 --> 00:00:42.075 line:92%
-You are a very busy perso

00:00:42.075 --> 00:00:45.245 size:84% position:42%
and, while we greatly
appreciate your efforts

00:00:45.245 --> 00:00:48.348
in trying to stop the tide
of voter suppression laws

00:00:48.348 --> 00:00:51.317 align:start size:94% position:6%
that are, obviously,
a huge problem right now,

00:00:51.317 --> 00:00:53.119 align:start size:94% position:6%
you also have time
to write books.

00:00:53.119 --> 00:00:55.488
This is very exciting because,
this is not your first novel

00:00:55.488 --> 00:00:59.459
but it is your first novel
with your actual name on it.

00:00:59.459 --> 00:01:01.728 align:start size:94% position:6%
You've written
under a pen name before.

00:01:01.728 --> 00:01:03.263 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm wondering --
obviously, you knew

00:01:03.263 --> 00:01:05.532 align:start size:94% position:6%
you were the author
of those books.

00:01:05.532 --> 00:01:07.300 align:start size:94% position:6%
Was it different,
writing a book,

00:01:07.300 --> 00:01:09.102 align:start size:94% position:6%
knowing that everyone
who picked it up

00:01:09.102 --> 00:01:12.105 align:start size:94% position:6%
would know it was written
by the Stacey Abrams?

00:01:12.105 --> 00:01:15.675
-No, I think what was differen
was knowing people might care.

00:01:15.675 --> 00:01:17.811 align:start size:94% position:6%
When I wrote the first
eight novels,

00:01:17.811 --> 00:01:20.780 align:start size:94% position:6%
Selena Montgomery was much mor
exciting than Stacey Abram

00:01:20.780 --> 00:01:24.017
and so I'm glad that peopl
will actually pick up a book

00:01:24.017 --> 00:01:24.884 line:92%
because my name is on it,

00:01:24.884 --> 00:01:27.153 align:start size:94% position:6%
instead of despite my name
being on it.

00:01:27.153 --> 00:01:29.856
-This is an idea that you
came up with 10 years ago

00:01:29.856 --> 00:01:32.325 align:start size:94% position:6%
and publishers passed
on it then.

00:01:32.325 --> 00:01:33.026 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
What was it?

00:01:33.026 --> 00:01:36.463 align:start size:94% position:6%
Did the times change?
Did the circumstances change

00:01:36.463 --> 00:01:37.730 line:92%
Were people just more excite

00:01:37.730 --> 00:01:40.133 align:start size:94% position:6%
that you wanted
to put your name on a book

00:01:40.133 --> 00:01:44.838
What changed that made this book
a book for today?

00:01:44.838 --> 00:01:48.808 align:start size:94% position:6%
-When I first proposed the boo
and had written it,

00:01:48.808 --> 00:01:49.742 line:92%
I had a corrupt president

00:01:49.742 --> 00:01:51.845 align:start size:94% position:6%
who was involved
in international intrigue

00:01:51.845 --> 00:01:54.114 align:start size:94% position:6%
and a swing justice
on the Supreme Court,

00:01:54.114 --> 00:01:55.582 align:start size:94% position:6%
who may decide
the fate of the world,

00:01:55.582 --> 00:01:58.051 size:81% position:41%
and that was dismissed
as being too absurdist

00:01:58.051 --> 00:02:00.253 align:start size:94% position:6%
and not quite
contemporary enough.

00:02:00.253 --> 00:02:02.722
So, you know, we had some
intervening activities

00:02:02.722 --> 00:02:05.325 size:81% position:41% line:92%
between 2008 and 2020,

00:02:05.325 --> 00:02:08.661 align:start size:94% position:6%
and so, the book
suddenly seemed relevant.

00:02:08.661 --> 00:02:10.697 align:start size:94% position:6%
-We talked
about "Queen's Gambit"

00:02:10.697 --> 00:02:11.631 line:92%
last time you were on the show

00:02:11.631 --> 00:02:14.300 align:start size:94% position:6%
and how wonderful
that television show is.

00:02:14.300 --> 00:02:17.036 align:start size:94% position:6%
There is a chess element
in this as well.

00:02:17.036 --> 00:02:17.871 line:92%
You want to make it clear

00:02:17.871 --> 00:02:20.473 align:start size:94% position:6%
you had your chess element
10 years ago.

00:02:20.473 --> 00:02:21.374 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-I did. I did.

00:02:21.374 --> 00:02:23.243 line:92%
Started writing this in 2008

00:02:23.243 --> 00:02:26.212 align:start size:94% position:6%
long before I knew
of the "Queen's Gambit."

00:02:26.212 --> 00:02:27.080 line:92%
-I also want to ask about this

00:02:27.080 --> 00:02:30.650 align:start size:94% position:6%
You have, I believe,
five siblings, is that right

00:02:30.650 --> 00:02:31.951 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
-And they work

00:02:31.951 --> 00:02:35.188 size:84% position:42%
in very diverse fields,
professional fields,

00:02:35.188 --> 00:02:38.725 align:start size:94% position:6%
and, yet, they all give yo
feedback on your books.

00:02:38.725 --> 00:02:41.161 align:start size:94% position:6%
Is this feedback
that you are open to?

00:02:41.161 --> 00:02:43.530 align:start size:94% position:6%
Do you like having sibling
like this?

00:02:43.530 --> 00:02:46.299 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I am grateful to them
when I ask,

00:02:46.299 --> 00:02:49.202 align:start size:94% position:6%
I am sometimes grateful
when they answer,

00:02:49.202 --> 00:02:53.873 align:start size:94% position:6%
but they're an incredible
phalanx of really smart people

00:02:53.873 --> 00:02:56.009 align:start size:94% position:6%
and that's much cheaper
than having to pay an expert

00:02:56.009 --> 00:02:58.278 align:start size:94% position:6%
to tell you things,
faster than Google.

00:02:58.278 --> 00:03:00.880
You get immediate feedback
you can ask more questions

00:03:00.880 --> 00:03:02.549 align:start size:94% position:6%
refine the issues,
and you don't have

00:03:02.549 --> 00:03:05.652 align:start size:94% position:6%
to press 1 or 2 to get to,
you know, an operator.

00:03:05.652 --> 00:03:07.554 line:92%
They just answer when I call

00:03:07.554 --> 00:03:09.822 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You have a federal judge
in the family?

00:03:09.822 --> 00:03:11.291 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's correct?
-I do.

00:03:11.291 --> 00:03:12.592 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Is it a biologist?

00:03:12.592 --> 00:03:16.496 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes. So Jeanine
is an evolutionary biologist

00:03:16.496 --> 00:03:18.565 line:92%
-These are very helpful fields

00:03:18.565 --> 00:03:20.667 align:start size:94% position:6%
for the kinds of books
you're writing.

00:03:20.667 --> 00:03:23.836 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Social worker,
an anthropologist.

00:03:23.836 --> 00:03:25.004 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
We run the gamut.

00:03:25.004 --> 00:03:26.940 size:88% position:44%
-Is it true -- I believe
it was the social worker

00:03:26.940 --> 00:03:29.509 align:start size:94% position:6%
that talked you
out of a car chase?

00:03:29.509 --> 00:03:32.378 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes!
He cut my scene.

00:03:32.378 --> 00:03:33.279 size:78% position:39% line:92%
I thought it was fun,

00:03:33.279 --> 00:03:36.983 align:start size:94% position:6%
but he literally thought
the scene took too long, so.

00:03:36.983 --> 00:03:37.884 line:92%
-Oh, he thought it was just --

00:03:37.884 --> 00:03:41.354 align:start size:94% position:6%
he just wanted you
to get to what was happening

00:03:41.354 --> 00:03:42.689 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Exactly.

00:03:42.689 --> 00:03:45.558 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I will say I love
a good car chase,

00:03:45.558 --> 00:03:47.927 align:start size:94% position:6%
but more on film.
-Yes.

00:03:47.927 --> 00:03:49.062 line:92%
-When I'm reading a car chase,

00:03:49.062 --> 00:03:50.096 align:start size:94% position:6%
I kind of want to see it
a little bit,

00:03:50.096 --> 00:03:53.032 align:start size:94% position:6%
so I'm going to side
with your brother on that one.

00:03:53.032 --> 00:03:54.234 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:03:54.234 --> 00:03:55.668 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:55.668 --> 00:03:57.937 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You guys also have
a family book club.

00:03:57.937 --> 00:04:01.241 align:start size:94% position:6%
Is this a deal where everybody
actually reads the books?

00:04:01.241 --> 00:04:03.543 align:start size:94% position:6%
-We do, and we can tell
if you haven't,

00:04:03.543 --> 00:04:05.545 align:start size:94% position:6%
so what happens is
we set a deadline

00:04:05.545 --> 00:04:09.482 size:84% position:42%
for doing the book club
and then someone calls.

00:04:09.482 --> 00:04:11.618 align:start size:94% position:6%
One of us will call
our older sister,

00:04:11.618 --> 00:04:13.586 align:start size:94% position:6%
who's responsible
for convening us,

00:04:13.586 --> 00:04:15.021 align:start size:94% position:6%
and somebody has to come u
with an excuse

00:04:15.021 --> 00:04:16.589 align:start size:94% position:6%
for why they didn't get it
done this week.

00:04:16.589 --> 00:04:19.792 align:start size:94% position:6%
You don't want to be the perso
who does it every time,

00:04:19.792 --> 00:04:20.827 size:88% position:44% line:92%
so you'll have this like

00:04:20.827 --> 00:04:23.997 align:start size:94% position:6%
phone tree of,
"Well, I did it last time!

00:04:23.997 --> 00:04:25.965 size:84% position:42%
And then, we get Andrea
to give us permission

00:04:25.965 --> 00:04:27.934 align:start size:94% position:6%
to put off the book club
for another week.

00:04:27.934 --> 00:04:28.701 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-[ Laughs ]

00:04:28.701 --> 00:04:31.704 align:start size:94% position:6%
Your mom, a librarian back
in the day, correct?

00:04:31.704 --> 00:04:34.874 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes. Correct.
-Does she participate as well?

00:04:34.874 --> 00:04:37.143 align:start size:94% position:6%
-She does not, so it's jus
a sibling book club

00:04:37.143 --> 00:04:39.479 align:start size:94% position:6%
and we've heard about the fact
that we are

00:04:39.479 --> 00:04:43.683 align:start size:94% position:6%
just a sibling book club
and we don't include my mother

00:04:43.683 --> 00:04:45.018 line:92%
so please don't bring it up.

00:04:45.018 --> 00:04:45.685 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:45.685 --> 00:04:48.454
-Is this an active choice,
to not have her participate?

00:04:48.454 --> 00:04:51.658
What do you think would go
wrong, if she was there?

00:04:51.658 --> 00:04:56.062 align:start size:94% position:6%
-There are six of us who hav
a robust conversation

00:04:56.062 --> 00:04:58.364 align:start size:94% position:6%
and we read
varying degrees of books

00:04:58.364 --> 00:05:01.734 align:start size:94% position:6%
and we don't circumscribe
our language, always,

00:05:01.734 --> 00:05:03.670 align:start size:94% position:6%
in our discussion
about plot points.

00:05:03.670 --> 00:05:07.373 align:start size:94% position:6%
My mother went from being
a librarian to being a pastor,

00:05:07.373 --> 00:05:08.608 align:start size:94% position:6%
so I will let you infer
from there

00:05:08.608 --> 00:05:10.443 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Laughs ]
-why there might be a proble

00:05:10.443 --> 00:05:12.612 align:start size:94% position:6%
with having her
on the call the whole time

00:05:12.612 --> 00:05:16.349
-Hey, you know, you've bee
a guest on this show a lot

00:05:16.349 --> 00:05:20.553 size:88% position:44%
and I was very touched
by something in the book

00:05:20.553 --> 00:05:24.824 align:start size:94% position:6%
because I know you're not
on only this late night show

00:05:24.824 --> 00:05:26.059 align:start size:94% position:6%
You've also been
on Stephen Colbert,

00:05:26.059 --> 00:05:29.896 size:88% position:44%
of whom I'm a great fan,
and this is really cool.

00:05:29.896 --> 00:05:31.564 size:78% position:39%
In the book, it says,
"Nigel rocked slowly.

00:05:31.564 --> 00:05:34.434 align:start size:94% position:6%
'The president wasn't please
with my press conference.

00:05:34.434 --> 00:05:37.704 size:84% position:42%
I'm booked on Colbert
for tonight's broadcast

00:05:37.704 --> 00:05:39.205 size:84% position:42% line:92%
and also Seth Meyers.'"

00:05:39.205 --> 00:05:40.406 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I just thought
it was so cool

00:05:40.406 --> 00:05:42.408 line:92%
that you mentioned us as well.

00:05:42.408 --> 00:05:44.944 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:44.944 --> 00:05:47.280 size:81% position:41% line:92%
Meant the world to me.

00:05:47.280 --> 00:05:48.614 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because my feelings would've
obviously, been hurt,

00:05:48.614 --> 00:05:51.384
if it would've been just lik
sort of exclusive to Stephen

00:05:51.384 --> 00:05:55.455
-You're anticipating -- look
there's going to be a show

00:05:55.455 --> 00:05:56.055 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
about the book.

00:05:56.055 --> 00:05:58.858
You assumed that I was jus
going to put both of you

00:05:58.858 --> 00:05:59.592 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
in competition.

00:05:59.592 --> 00:06:01.361 line:92%
I like to keep things separate

00:06:01.361 --> 00:06:01.994 size:75% position:38% line:92%
-Well, this is true.

00:06:01.994 --> 00:06:04.063 align:start size:94% position:6%
I want to talk
about this as well.

00:06:04.063 --> 00:06:07.700 align:start size:94% position:6%
The book is,
we just found out today,

00:06:07.700 --> 00:06:08.601 line:92%
going to be a television show.

00:06:08.601 --> 00:06:12.238 align:start size:94% position:6%
Is that something that
you had ever thought possible,

00:06:12.238 --> 00:06:14.841 align:start size:94% position:6%
when you were first
sitting down to write it?

00:06:14.841 --> 00:06:15.475 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-No. I mean, look,

00:06:15.475 --> 00:06:17.210 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was surprised
somebody finally published it,

00:06:17.210 --> 00:06:20.613 align:start size:94% position:6%
so getting a TV show
in this century is awesome

00:06:20.613 --> 00:06:22.615 align:start size:94% position:6%
But, no, I love television
as you know,

00:06:22.615 --> 00:06:25.685 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I'm just very excited
that Working Title

00:06:25.685 --> 00:06:28.588
and Universal are excited
about doing this with me.

00:06:28.588 --> 00:06:32.058 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I feel like a difference
between this visit

00:06:32.058 --> 00:06:33.926 align:start size:94% position:6%
to you on our show
and previous times

00:06:33.926 --> 00:06:36.829 align:start size:94% position:6%
is your backdrop now
seems very professional to me.

00:06:36.829 --> 00:06:38.831
-Oh, thank you.
-I feel like I've seen you a lot

00:06:38.831 --> 00:06:42.502 align:start size:94% position:6%
in your home, maybe in sort of
a nondescript office,

00:06:42.502 --> 00:06:44.771 align:start size:94% position:6%
and now, this is very showbiz.
It's amazing.

00:06:44.771 --> 00:06:46.439 align:start size:94% position:6%
The minute your book
gets optioned,

00:06:46.439 --> 00:06:47.707 size:88% position:44% line:92%
look at your background.

00:06:47.707 --> 00:06:49.275 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:06:49.275 --> 00:06:52.879 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I've also been double vaxxed,
man, so I can go outside.

00:06:52.879 --> 00:06:56.015 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:06:56.015 --> 00:06:58.284 line:92%
-Can you tell us any reaso

00:06:58.284 --> 00:07:01.954 align:start size:94% position:6%
to not be pessimistic
and depressed

00:07:01.954 --> 00:07:06.459
about how effectively Republican
state legislatures seem

00:07:06.459 --> 00:07:10.029 align:start size:94% position:6%
to be passing
voter suppression bills?

00:07:10.029 --> 00:07:12.832
-I think we should be concerned,
we should pay attention,

00:07:12.832 --> 00:07:15.001 align:start size:94% position:6%
but we've also been
very effective.

00:07:15.001 --> 00:07:19.739
We've seen some of the worst
pieces come out of those bills

00:07:19.739 --> 00:07:22.008 align:start size:94% position:6%
and, even though
they continue to pass,

00:07:22.008 --> 00:07:23.476 align:start size:94% position:6%
more and more people
are aware of it.

00:07:23.476 --> 00:07:25.678 align:start size:94% position:6%
And we still have time
for Congress to take actions

00:07:25.678 --> 00:07:27.146 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it's working
on it right now

00:07:27.146 --> 00:07:31.050
and I believe that we can
actually have democracy

00:07:31.050 --> 00:07:33.453 size:81% position:41%
that is free and fair
and accessible to all,

00:07:33.453 --> 00:07:35.354 line:92%
so, I'm going to keep pushing.

00:07:35.354 --> 00:07:37.690
-You have been --
we've shown clips of you here --

00:07:37.690 --> 00:07:39.625 align:start size:94% position:6%
very effective
when you've gone

00:07:39.625 --> 00:07:41.027 line:92%
in front of Senate committees,

00:07:41.027 --> 00:07:43.095 align:start size:94% position:6%
when you've gone in front
of House committees.

00:07:43.095 --> 00:07:47.500
How much preparation do you have
to put into those appearance

00:07:47.500 --> 00:07:50.036 align:start size:94% position:6%
and how much of it is just
at this point,

00:07:50.036 --> 00:07:54.006 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know your stuff and there'
nothing to worry about?

00:07:54.006 --> 00:07:55.608 line:92%
-I'm generally up to speed

00:07:55.608 --> 00:07:57.710 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, before I did
the last Senate appearance

00:07:57.710 --> 00:08:01.347
I did ask my team to give me
as much detail as they could

00:08:01.347 --> 00:08:05.485 align:start size:94% position:6%
Luckily, I was able to retai
that information in time

00:08:05.485 --> 00:08:10.490
for some questions that wanted
sort of a list of challenges

00:08:10.490 --> 00:08:13.960 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I am incredibly grateful
to the Fair Fight team.

00:08:13.960 --> 00:08:15.061 line:92%
They keep me well prepped.

00:08:15.061 --> 00:08:16.362 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, they're
like my siblings,

00:08:16.362 --> 00:08:19.699 align:start size:94% position:6%
only, we pay them
to do their work.

00:08:19.699 --> 00:08:22.368 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Now that you are known
as, obviously,

00:08:22.368 --> 00:08:24.337 size:75% position:38%
not just an advocate
for voting rights,

00:08:24.337 --> 00:08:26.506 align:start size:94% position:6%
but also as an author
of fiction,

00:08:26.506 --> 00:08:29.609
do you feel like people in D.C
are now a little worried that,

00:08:29.609 --> 00:08:33.813 align:start size:94% position:6%
if they behave in a way that i
both bad and memorable,

00:08:33.813 --> 00:08:38.050 align:start size:94% position:6%
they will become fictionalized
in one of your books?

00:08:38.050 --> 00:08:40.553
-Given that my colleagues
at the state legislature

00:08:40.553 --> 00:08:41.687 align:start size:94% position:6%
occasionally found themselve
in the book

00:08:41.687 --> 00:08:46.125
and the current speaker of the
House for the Georgia House is

00:08:46.125 --> 00:08:47.527 line:92%
in "While Justice Sleeps" --

00:08:47.527 --> 00:08:49.795 line:92%
he knew about it 10 years ago,

00:08:49.795 --> 00:08:50.763 size:81% position:41% line:92%
he's still in there --

00:08:50.763 --> 00:08:52.598 align:start size:94% position:6%
I just warn people,
"You may be in the book

00:08:52.598 --> 00:08:53.733 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
and you might die."

00:08:53.733 --> 00:08:54.800 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:08:54.800 --> 00:08:55.535 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-That's very nice.

00:08:55.535 --> 00:08:56.869 align:start size:94% position:6%
But that doesn't
necessarily mean --

00:08:56.869 --> 00:08:58.971 align:start size:94% position:6%
Now, if someone is represented
in one of your books

00:08:58.971 --> 00:09:02.275
and they die, that sometimes
is just you serving the plot

00:09:02.275 --> 00:09:04.277 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Absolutely.
-That is not a negative commen

00:09:04.277 --> 00:09:05.144 size:78% position:39% line:92%
on their personality.

00:09:05.144 --> 00:09:06.846 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Absolutely. Or they were
in the car chase

00:09:06.846 --> 00:09:08.347 align:start size:94% position:6%
and they got cut out,
so, there you go.

00:09:08.347 --> 00:09:11.384 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, a fate worse than death
is getting cut out,

00:09:11.384 --> 00:09:13.052 align:start size:94% position:6%
which, thank God,
didn't happen to me

00:09:13.052 --> 00:09:15.955 line:92%
because I made it in the book.

00:09:15.955 --> 00:09:17.223 line:92%
There it is right there, proof

00:09:17.223 --> 00:09:21.694 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
See? It's so great.

00:09:21.694 --> 00:09:23.129 line:92%
Where do you do your writing

00:09:23.129 --> 00:09:24.664 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because I feel like
that's the thing

00:09:24.664 --> 00:09:26.432 align:start size:94% position:6%
that is most interesting
to people

00:09:26.432 --> 00:09:29.802
who can't believe that anyon
could sit down and write a book.

00:09:29.802 --> 00:09:32.672 line:92%
What is your perfect situation

00:09:32.672 --> 00:09:35.374 line:92%
-So I have a secretary desk.

00:09:35.374 --> 00:09:37.843 align:start size:94% position:6%
You pull it out
and it lays flat.

00:09:37.843 --> 00:09:40.646 size:75% position:38%
Put my laptop on top
and start writing.

00:09:40.646 --> 00:09:42.515 size:88% position:44% line:92%
Or my dining room table.

00:09:42.515 --> 00:09:44.750 align:start size:94% position:6%
Depends on how good
the light is,

00:09:44.750 --> 00:09:46.852 align:start size:94% position:6%
whether I can actually get
to the desk

00:09:46.852 --> 00:09:48.487 line:92%
because it's covered with stuff.

00:09:48.487 --> 00:09:51.090
Wherever my computer will fit,
that is where I sit to write

00:09:51.090 --> 00:09:55.061 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And, when you write,
do you tend to do a lot at onc

00:09:55.061 --> 00:09:58.731 align:start size:94% position:6%
or are you someone who grabs
an hour here or there?

00:09:58.731 --> 00:10:01.701 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because I find I need a lo
of uninterrupted time,

00:10:01.701 --> 00:10:03.603 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
just to percolate.

00:10:03.603 --> 00:10:06.939 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I usually have half a day
to a day set aside

00:10:06.939 --> 00:10:10.042 align:start size:94% position:6%
I will schedule to write
because, for me,

00:10:10.042 --> 00:10:12.678 align:start size:94% position:6%
writer's block isn't
that I can't think of it.

00:10:12.678 --> 00:10:14.046 line:92%
It's, "I don't want to do it

00:10:14.046 --> 00:10:15.081 line:92%
I don't like words anymore

00:10:15.081 --> 00:10:16.882 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't want to write it.
Never mind,"

00:10:16.882 --> 00:10:19.085 align:start size:94% position:6%
and then I've got to give
myself time to get past that

00:10:19.085 --> 00:10:21.621 align:start size:94% position:6%
and then to sit down
and do my work.

00:10:21.621 --> 00:10:25.524 size:84% position:42%
-And are there times
where you sort of break

00:10:25.524 --> 00:10:26.826 line:92%
maybe a plot problem you had

00:10:26.826 --> 00:10:31.364
or you find a way of sayin
something that delights you?

00:10:31.364 --> 00:10:32.932 size:84% position:42%
Do you celebrate it all
while you're writing

00:10:32.932 --> 00:10:34.767 align:start size:94% position:6%
or do you know in the moment
like, "Oh, yeah,

00:10:34.767 --> 00:10:37.703 align:start size:94% position:6%
this is a really good one,
right here"?

00:10:37.703 --> 00:10:38.371 size:81% position:41% line:92%
-No, I will get happy.

00:10:38.371 --> 00:10:40.272 align:start size:94% position:6%
I had one book,
not "While Justice Sleeps" -

00:10:40.272 --> 00:10:42.575 align:start size:94% position:6%
I had another book
where my character

00:10:42.575 --> 00:10:44.677 align:start size:94% position:6%
was supposed to be going
out onto a cliff

00:10:44.677 --> 00:10:47.713
and she ended up in a cave and I
had no idea why she was ther

00:10:47.713 --> 00:10:49.982 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it took like three day
to figure it out.

00:10:49.982 --> 00:10:51.584 align:start size:94% position:6%
When I realized
why she was there,

00:10:51.584 --> 00:10:54.887 align:start size:94% position:6%
it made perfect sense,
so I sometimes have to wai

00:10:54.887 --> 00:10:58.024 align:start size:94% position:6%
for the plot to reveal itsel
to me in greater detail.

00:10:58.024 --> 00:11:01.427
-And how much do they come
to you with the cover of a book?

00:11:01.427 --> 00:11:05.164
Like how many different versions
do you see before you sign off

00:11:05.164 --> 00:11:08.267
-This was actually the ver
first cover they recommended

00:11:08.267 --> 00:11:11.737 align:start size:94% position:6%
I thought it was evocative
of the story

00:11:11.737 --> 00:11:15.474
and it was really awesome
to see my name on the book

00:11:15.474 --> 00:11:17.276 line:92%
But I really loved the colors.

00:11:17.276 --> 00:11:18.978 align:start size:94% position:6%
I just thought it was
a really well done cover

00:11:18.978 --> 00:11:23.215 align:start size:94% position:6%
and the team at Doubleday
has been amazing to work with.

00:11:23.215 --> 00:11:24.383 line:92%
-On the Selena Montgomery books,

00:11:24.383 --> 00:11:27.787 align:start size:94% position:6%
was there no author photo
on the back of the book jacket

00:11:27.787 --> 00:11:30.556
-Oh, no, no. My face is
in every one of my books.

00:11:30.556 --> 00:11:34.960
When I say that nobody cared
this was not self-deprecation.

00:11:34.960 --> 00:11:36.762 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Just nobody cared.

00:11:36.762 --> 00:11:39.765 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:11:39.765 --> 00:11:41.901 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It was something like this,
but just, right here,

00:11:41.901 --> 00:11:44.370 line:92%
it said "Selena Montgomery"?

00:11:44.370 --> 00:11:45.905 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yes.

00:11:45.905 --> 00:11:47.740 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then, if you look
at the copyright,

00:11:47.740 --> 00:11:49.008 size:88% position:44% line:92%
it said "Stacey Abrams."

00:11:49.008 --> 00:11:49.709 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:11:49.709 --> 00:11:50.976 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I feel like they're going
to pull you

00:11:50.976 --> 00:11:51.777 line:92%
in front of the Senate for that.

00:11:51.777 --> 00:11:53.145 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Laughs ]
-I feel like they're going
to have

00:11:53.145 --> 00:11:54.980 align:start size:94% position:6%
a lot of questions about that.
[ Laughter ]

00:11:54.980 --> 00:11:57.616 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I will refer them
to this show for answers

00:11:57.616 --> 00:11:59.018 align:start size:94% position:6%
because that's
what everyone should do.

00:11:59.018 --> 00:12:02.555
-Oh, well, it'll be nice for you
to talk about this show.

00:12:02.555 --> 00:12:04.023 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:12:04.023 --> 00:12:07.893 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I will talk about this show
so much from now on.

00:12:07.893 --> 00:12:09.462 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Stacey,
if that's your real name,

00:12:09.462 --> 00:12:12.498 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
it is always a delight
to see you.

00:12:12.498 --> 00:12:14.233 line:92%
Congratulations on the book.

00:12:14.233 --> 00:12:16.135 size:88% position:44%
-Seth, thank you so much
and thank you for being

00:12:16.135 --> 00:12:19.171 align:start size:94% position:6%
so generous
and such a tremendous show

00:12:19.171 --> 00:12:20.740 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:12:20.740 --> 00:12:21.440 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Nice try.

00:12:21.440 --> 00:12:23.342 align:start size:94% position:6%
"While Justice Sleeps"
is available now

00:12:23.342 --> 00:12:25.244 align:start size:94% position:6%
wherever books are sold,
but please support

00:12:25.244 --> 00:12:27.980 align:start size:94% position:6%
your local
and independent bookstores

